{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9dafd971-df86-4d24-ac72-7929487727be","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-862a372fb4899c25","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-r_cjj247/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md","content":"# Eliminate non-validated crypto in KServe serving-stack images\n\n## Description\n\nRemediate the KServe serving-stack images so that, on FIPS-enabled OpenShift\nclusters, the model serving request path uses only validated cryptographic\nmodules. This epic covers the audit of cryptographic-library linkage across the\nKServe images, the replacement of non-validated crypto usage in the request\npath, and the verification that models served through the stack work correctly\nunder FIPS mode.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enumerate every KServe image shipped as part of the model serving stack.\n- Audit each image's linked cryptographic libraries and identify all\n  non-validated crypto usage in the serving request path.\n- Replace the identified non-validated crypto usages with validated crypto\n  modules and rebuild the affected images.\n- Re-audit the rebuilt images to confirm no non-validated crypto remains in the\n  request path.\n- Validate that model serving (InferenceService request handling) works\n  correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster in the deployment modes the\n  stack supports.\n- Keep all image builds green in the existing build pipeline.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented crypto-module inventory exists for every KServe image in the\n  serving stack, and every non-validated usage in the request path is\n  identified. (pass/fail: inventory exists and is complete for all enumerated\n  images)\n- A re-audit of the rebuilt images shows zero non-validated crypto usage in the\n  serving request path.\n- InferenceServices serve inference requests correctly on a FIPS-enabled\n  OpenShift cluster, verified by functional tests against served models.\n- All rebuilt KServe images pass their builds in the existing build pipeline.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled\n  clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the\n  request path) — this epic delivers that requirement for the KServe images.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The number of affected images and linkage sites is established by the audit;\n  the strategy estimates \"several images\". If the audit finds materially more,\n  re-split this epic along image or sub-system lines (see the decomposition\n  summary's re-split trigger).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45428,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ca1c42f513e3b4b","agent_id":"a499bb043a75f3f2e","session_id":"06dfd5f6-e298-413b-a31d-879a10490586","uuid":"cdb07a25-8043-46ff-b2b4-4a81486d3847","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:51:10.631Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
