{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b06c7fa5-6107-4fb7-8971-6818c670a249","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-83b60b615860575e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-r_cjj247/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E003.md","content":"# CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds\n\n## Description\n\nAdd a gating CI check that fails any model-serving-stack image build which\nreintroduces non-validated crypto usage, so that FIPS compliance cannot regress\nonce the remediated images ship. The check is developed in parallel with the\nimage remediation work; its coupling to that work is expressed through\nacceptance criteria, not through a scheduling dependency.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement detection of non-validated crypto-library linkage in\n  serving-stack image builds (the detection rules align with the\n  validated-module inventory established by the serving-stack image audit).\n- Wire the check into the build pipeline so it runs on every serving-stack\n  image build.\n- Make the check gating: a build that fails it cannot merge/ship.\n- Provide a negative test fixture (a build that links a known non-validated\n  crypto library) to prove the check fires, and a clean build to prove it\n  passes.\n- Time the activation of the gating behavior so it does not fail builds that\n  predate the remediated images (advisory first, gating once remediation\n  lands).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The check runs automatically on every serving-stack image build in CI.\n- A build that links non-validated crypto in the request path fails the check,\n  demonstrated by the negative test fixture.\n- A build using only validated crypto modules passes the check.\n- The check is gating, not advisory, at activation time.\n- The check's detection rules cover every class of non-validated crypto usage\n  identified by the serving-stack image audit (this criterion, not a DAG edge,\n  is what couples the check to the remediation's findings).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: CI enforces FIPS regressions — a gating check fails any\n  serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46724,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ca1c42f513e3b4b","agent_id":"a499bb043a75f3f2e","session_id":"06dfd5f6-e298-413b-a31d-879a10490586","uuid":"f90a4dd7-bf67-4194-9380-24719ef43651","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:51:25.932Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
