{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa64305ff16934c5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n3\ttitle: CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAdd a gating CI check that fails any model-serving-stack image build which\n34\treintroduces non-validated crypto usage, so that FIPS compliance cannot regress\n35\tonce the remediated images ship. The check is developed in parallel with the\n36\timage remediation work; its coupling to that work is expressed through\n37\tacceptance criteria, not through a scheduling dependency.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Implement detection of non-validated crypto-library linkage in\n42\t  serving-stack image builds (the detection rules align with the\n43\t  validated-module inventory established by the serving-stack image audit).\n44\t- Wire the check into the build pipeline so it runs on every serving-stack\n45\t  image build.\n46\t- Make the check gating: a build that fails it cannot merge/ship.\n47\t- Provide a negative test fixture (a build that links a known non-validated\n48\t  crypto library) to prove the check fires, and a clean build to prove it\n49\t  passes.\n50\t- Time the activation of the gating behavior so it does not fail builds that\n51\t  predate the remediated images (advisory first, gating once remediation\n52\t  lands).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The check runs automatically on every serving-stack image build in CI.\n57\t- A build that links non-validated crypto in the request path fails the check,\n58\t  demonstrated by the negative test fixture.\n59\t- A build using only validated crypto modules passes the check.\n60\t- The check is gating, not advisory, at activation time.\n61\t- The check's detection rules cover every class of non-validated crypto usage\n62\t  identified by the serving-stack image audit (this criterion, not a DAG edge,\n63\t  is what couples the check to the remediation's findings).\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: CI enforces FIPS regressions — a gating check fails any\n68\t  serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-874d7e082a7ef236","agent_id":"abf0dd22a7ff81c6c","session_id":"06dfd5f6-e298-413b-a31d-879a10490586","uuid":"2f822576-0905-4842-bcd4-c4e9346d9c97","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:53:15.567Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa64305ff16934c5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
