{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b163edfa0d1a657a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E004\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and submission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 0\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 1\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and submission\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tAssemble the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model serving\n36\tstack — the crypto-module inventory, build attestations, and test results —\n37\tand submit it through the mandatory security review board to the external\n38\taccredited certification lab. This epic's engineering deliverable ends at a\n39\tcomplete, submitted, triaged package; the certification decision and the lab's\n40\treview timeline are outside its control.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Aggregate the per-image crypto-module inventories produced by the serving\n45\t  stack's FIPS remediation into a single module inventory covering every\n46\t  in-scope serving-stack image.\n47\t- Collect the build attestations produced by the serving-stack build pipelines\n48\t  for every remediated image (included as content of the package; no pipeline\n49\t  scheduling dependency is implied).\n50\t- Collect the test results demonstrating correct operation on FIPS-enabled\n51\t  OpenShift clusters with validated crypto modules.\n52\t- Assemble the package in the form required by the security review board and\n53\t  the certification lab's submission requirements.\n54\t- Drive the package through security review board sign-off and submit it to\n55\t  the external certification lab; confirm the submission is triaged.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- The evidence package contains a module inventory covering every in-scope\n60\t  serving-stack image, with validated/non-validated status per module.\n61\t- The evidence package includes the build attestations produced by the build\n62\t  pipelines for every remediated serving-stack image.\n63\t- The evidence package includes the FIPS-cluster test results for every\n64\t  remediated serving-stack image.\n65\t- The evidence package is submitted through the security review board to the\n66\t  external certification lab, and the submission is triaged/acknowledged by\n67\t  the lab.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build\n72\t  attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security\n73\t    review board to the external certification lab.\n74\t\n75\t## Risks / Notes\n76\t\n77\t- The accredited lab's historical turnaround is six to nine months, and the\n78\t  security review board signs off at defined milestones on its own cadence.\n79\t  Both are externally controlled schedule constraints that engineering effort\n80\t  cannot compress; they are recorded here as risks, not as acceptance\n81\t  criteria. The certification grant itself is likewise outside this epic's\n82\t  deliverable.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-874d7e082a7ef236","agent_id":"abf0dd22a7ff81c6c","session_id":"06dfd5f6-e298-413b-a31d-879a10490586","uuid":"28c03b7d-49f2-48cd-a911-3fda8110891e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:53:16.122Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b163edfa0d1a657a","permission_decision":{"decision":"ac