idance** — how a user or support engineer can confirm the\n54\t  deployed serving stack is using validated crypto modules, aligned with the\n55\t  shipped evidence and the CI regression gate.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Published documentation states the FIPS support posture of the model serving\n60\t  stack and the cluster prerequisites (HLR-4's substance).\n61\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior of the\n62\t  remediated serving stack — reviewed by engineers who worked on the FIPS\n63\t  remediation, validation, and evidence effort, so no statement contradicts\n64\t  what was built or submitted.\n65\t- Documentation topics cover every item in the Scope outline above.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- **HLR-4 (P2)**: Documentation states the FIPS support posture and cluster\n70\t  prerequisites.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-874d7e082a7ef236","agent_id":"abf0dd22a7ff81c6c","session_id":"06dfd5f6-e298-413b-a31d-879a10490586","uuid":"f89337c8-d0bf-43f8-9741-a71e67f87301","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:53:16.757Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b13e02824baa68b0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
