{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b807ae9cdadeee3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9013\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: HLR Coverage\n9\t  description: HLR-1 requires no non-validated crypto in the request path for all\n10\t    serving-stack images, and the problem statement asserts the serving data plane\n11\t    links non-validated crypto today; per .context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md\n12\t    the model-execution data plane is Serving Runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit), which\n13\t    has no epic. Health Warning 3 flags this but frames it conditionally (if those\n14\t    runtime images also link non-validated crypto). Obtain the strategy author boundary\n15\t    confirmation before execution; if Serving Runtimes are in scope, add the remediation\n16\t    epic or record an explicit deferral with justification.\n17\t- severity: minor\n18\t  criterion: Epic Boundaries\n19\t  description: 'E003 is assigned component KServe / team RHOAI Serving, but its ACs\n20\t    require the gating check to run on every serving-stack image build, which includes\n21\t    Platform Operator builds owned by RHOAI Platform Operators. Clarify the cross-team\n22\t    wiring: either scope E003 ACs to KServe builds only or explicitly note the operator-pipeline\n23\t    wiring as coordinated work with RHOAI Platform Operators.'\n24\t- severity: minor\n25\t  criterion: Acceptance Criteria Quality\n26\t  description: E004 final AC includes the clause that the submission is triaged/acknowledged\n27\t    by the lab — an outcome controlled by the external certification lab and beyond\n28\t    HLR-2, which ends at submission through the security review board. Move that clause\n29\t    to Risks/Notes and end the AC at submission.\n30\terror: null\n31\t---\n32\t## Review Summary\n33\t\n34\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n35\tRecommend