{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9464a36d4f1988c2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition: RHAISTRAT-9013 — FIPS 140-3 compliance for the model serving stack\n11\t\n12\t## Epic List\n13\t\n14\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n15\t|-------|-------|-----|------|----------|\n16\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E001 | Eliminate non-validated crypto in KServe serving-stack images | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n17\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 | Eliminate non-validated crypto in Platform Operator images | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operators | P0 |\n18\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 | CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P1 |\n19\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 | FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and submission | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n20\t| RHAISTRAT-9013-E005 | Document the serving-stack FIPS support posture | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n21\t\n22\tPriorities: E001/E002 inherit P0 from HLR-1; E004 is P0 from HLR-2. E003 stays P1\n23\t(HLR-3): it enables only the documentation epic, and edges into a `docs-authoring`\n24\tepic do not trigger priority inheritance. E005's P0 comes from the\n25\t`docs-authoring` priority exception — the strategy frontmatter priority is\n26\tCritical, which maps to P0 — not from HLR-4's P2 label (see Health Warnings).\n27\t\n28\t## Dependency DAG\n29\t\n30\t```mermaid\n31\tgraph TD\n32\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9013-E001 KServe image FIPS remediation] --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 evidence package and submission]\n33\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 Platform Operator image FIPS remediation] --> E004\n34\t    E001 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9013-E005 FIPS documentation]\n35\t    E002 --> E005\n36\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 CI FIPS regression gate] --> E005\n37\t    E004 --> E005\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t## DAG Justification\n41\t\n42\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n43\t|------|------|-----------|\n44\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 13 | The evidence package is assembled from deliverables the KServe remediation produces (per-image module inventory, FIPS-cluster test results). It cannot be complete before those artifacts exist, so the consumer is serial after the producer. |\n45\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 13 | Same: the operator-image remediation's inventory and test results are content of the evidence package. |\n46\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 | `docs-authoring` epic blocked by every Implementation epic; docs describe what was built. |\n47\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n48\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n49\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | Same. Documentation of the FIPS posture also reflects the submitted evidence package. |\n50\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Different components in different repos, no shared artifacts — remediation work proceeds in parallel. |\n51\t| E003 ∥ E001/E002 (no edge) | Rule 13 | The regression check's validated-module list is a configuration reference filled in at activation time; the coupling is expressed as acceptance criteria on the check (its detection rules must cover every class of non-validated usage found by the serving-stack image audit), never as a DAG edge. |\n52\t| E004 ∥ build pipelines (no edge) | Rule 13 | Build attestations consumed as content: the evidence package carries an AC that it includes the signed attestations produced by the serving-stack build pipelines, not a dependency on any pipeline epic. |\n53\t| E003 ∥ E004 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Independent deliverables; HLR-2's package does not include CI-enforcement evidence. |\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n56\t\n57\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epic(s) |\n58\t|-----|----------|------------------------|---------|\n59\t| HLR-1 | P0 | All serving-stack images run on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules | RHAISTRAT-9013-E001, RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 |\n60\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Compliance evidence package assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab | RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 |\n61\t| HLR-3 | P1 | CI gating check fails any serving-stack build reintroducing non-validated crypto | RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 |\n62\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation states the FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites | RHAISTRAT-9013-E005 |\n63\t\n64\tAll four HLRs are covered; none is orphaned. No epic maps to HLRs at multiple\n65\tpriority levels, so no bundling flags are needed: HLR-3 (P1) is a distinct,\n66\tindependently valuable capability on a separate surface (build-pipeline CI\n67\tconfiguration) from the HLR-1 image remediation, and HLR-4 (P2) is substantive\n68\tcontent authoring, which is a separate work stream by Rule 5's work-product\n69\tboundary — both are split, not bundled.\n70\t\n71\tHLR-1 note: \"all serving-stack images\" is scoped per the strategy's Affected\n72\tComponents list — the KServe images (E001) and the Platform Operator images\n73\t(E002). The Serving Runtime images (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit), which\n74\t`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md` identifies as\n75\tthe model-execution data plane, are explicitly deferred — see Health Warning 3.\n76\t\n77\tHLR-3 note: E003 delivers the CI gate for KServe serving-stack image builds in\n78\tthe pipelines owned by RHOAI Serving; wiring the gate into the Platform\n79\tOperator build pipeline is coordinated work with RHOAI Platform Operators and\n80\tis recorded as a risk on E003, since that pipeline is owned by a different\n81\tteam than E003's.\n82\t\n83\t## Health Warnings\n84\t\n85\t1. **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking).** The strategy has no Impacted\n86\t   Teams table, no per-component change descriptions or owners, no Dependencies\n87\t   table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no Non-Functional\n88\t   Requirements. Decomposition proceeded from the HLR table, the Affected\n89\t   Components list, and the problem statement.\n90\t2. **Team assignments are assumptions.** KServe epics are assigned to RHOAI\n91\t   Serving (corroborated by the KServe architecture-context file, which lists\n92\t   RHOAI Serving as owning team). No source names an owner for Platform Operator\n93\t   or for documentation; E002 is assigned to RHOAI Platform Operators and E005 to\n94\t   RHOAI Serving as best-effort defaults. Verify before scheduling.\n95\t3. **Serving Runtimes explicitly deferred under HLR-1 (scope boundary).** The\n96\t   problem statement asserts as present fact that \"KServe components and the\n97\t   serving data plane link non-validated crypto libraries\", and the KServe\n98\t   architecture-context file\n99\t   (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`) names\n100\t   Serving Runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit) as the model-execution data\n101\t   plane. The strategy's Affected Components list, however, declares only\n102\t   KServe and Platform Operator in scope. **Deferral:** no epic in this\n103\t   decomposition remediates the Serving Runtime images. Justification: the\n104\t   strategy's declared scope is the KServe and Platform Operator images, and\n105\t   remediating the runtime images is a separate body of work requiring its own\n106\t   audit, remediation, and evidence; folding it in would exceed the declared\n107\t   scope and the team assignments this decomposition relies on. Consequence:\n108\t   HLR-1's \"all serving-stack images\" is satisfied here only for the KServe\n109\t   and Platform Operator images — because the problem statement asserts the\n110\t   serving data plane links non-validated crypto today, a follow-up strategy\n111\t   covering the Serving Runtime images is required for the serving data plane\n112\t   as a whole to meet HLR-1. Confirm this boundary with the strategy author\n113\t   before execution; if the deferral is not intended, add a Serving Runtimes\n114\t   remediation epic mirroring E001.\n115\t4. **Platform Operator has no architecture-context file.** It is treated as an\n116\t   existing platform component (it is in the canonical RHAI component list and\n117\t   is the component that installs the stack) rather than triggering the\n118\t   new-component onboarding chain: this strategy hardens images of existing\n119\t   components and describes no provisioning. Its `architecture_claims` signal is\n120\t   scored 0 (no context file covers it). Recommend adding an architecture-context\n121\t   file for Platform Operator.\n122\t5. **External process gates are not modeled as work.** The accredited lab's\n123\t   historical six-to-nine-month turnaround and the security review board's\n124\t   cadence are externally controlled schedule constraints. They are recorded as\n125\t   risks on the evidence-package epic, not as epics, DAG edges, or acceptance\n126\t   criteria — the engineering-controlled completion point is a complete package\n127\t   submitted through the review board to the lab. The lab's triage of the\n128\t   submission and the certification decision itself are outside the strategy's\n129\t   control.\n130\t6. **E001 may run above the ~2-week epic-size guideline.** It deliberately\n131\t   bundles the crypto-linkage audit and the remediation of all KServe images as\n132\t   one logical change (splitting would fragment a single mechanical pass over\n133\t   one surface and duplicate the audit). Re-split trigger: re-split E001 along\n134\t   image or sub-system lines if the audit finds materially more affected images\n135\t   or crypto-linkage sites than the strategy's \"several images\" estimate\n136\t   suggests. The same trigger applies to E002.\n137\t\n138\t## Tiered Delivery\n139\t\n140\tThe external dependency here (the accredited certification lab) is a process\n141\tgate, not an upstream code dependency, so it does not create an upstream epic or\n142\ta DAG split. Tiered value still applies:\n143\t\n144\t- **Tier 1 (independent of lab timing):** E001, E002 (FIPS-capable images),\n145\t  E003 (regression protection), and E005 (documented posture) all deliver user\n146\t  value — serving-stack images that run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters —\n147\t  whether or not certification has completed.\n148\t- **Tier 2 (externally gated):** E004's submission and the eventual certification\n149\t  outcome depend on lab and review-board scheduling that engineering cannot\n150\t  compress. The decomposition isolates this in E004 so Tier 1 work is never\n151\t  blocked by it.\n152\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba6bdb076c1a8734","agent_id":"aa3a3d7aa4fa82aba","session_id":"06dfd5f6-e298-413b-a31d-879a10490586","uuid":"986cde06-3e2e-4a57-96e6-98ceaae20160","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:00:48.162Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9464a36d4f1988c2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
