{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d97b3e13daa5439","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: Eliminate non-validated crypto in KServe serving-stack images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: -1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Eliminate non-validated crypto in KServe serving-stack images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tRemediate the KServe serving-stack images so that, on FIPS-enabled OpenShift\n34\tclusters, the model serving request path uses only validated cryptographic\n35\tmodules. This epic covers the audit of cryptographic-library linkage across the\n36\tKServe images, the replacement of non-validated crypto usage in the request\n37\tpath, and the verification that models served through the stack work correctly\n38\tunder FIPS mode.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Enumerate every KServe image shipped as part of the model serving stack.\n43\t- Audit each image's linked cryptographic libraries and identify all\n44\t  non-validated crypto usage in the serving request path.\n45\t- Replace the identified non-validated crypto usages with validated crypto\n46\t  modules and rebuild the affected images.\n47\t- Re-audit the rebuilt images to confirm no non-validated crypto remains in the\n48\t  request path.\n49\t- Validate that model serving (InferenceService request handling) works\n50\t  correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster in the deployment modes the\n51\t  stack supports.\n52\t- Keep all image builds green in the existing build pipeline.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A documented crypto-module inventory exists for every KServe image in the\n57\t  serving stack, and every non-validated usage in the request path is\n58\t  identified. (pass/fail: inventory exists and is complete for all enumerated\n59\t  images)\n60\t- A re-audit of the rebuilt images shows zero non-validated crypto usage in the\n61\t  serving request path.\n62\t- InferenceServices serve inference requests correctly on a FIPS-enabled\n63\t  OpenShift cluster, verified by functional tests against served models.\n64\t- All rebuilt KServe images pass their builds in the existing build pipeline.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled\n69\t  clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the\n70\t  request path) — this epic delivers that requirement for the KServe images.\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- The number of affected images and linkage sites is established by the audit;\n75\t  the strategy estimates \"several images\". If the audit finds materially more,\n76\t  re-split this epic along image or sub-system lines (see the decomposition\n77\t  summary's re-split trigger).\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba6bdb076c1a8734","agent_id":"aa3a3d7aa4fa82aba","session_id":"06dfd5f6-e298-413b-a31d-879a10490586","uuid":"a3f331b5-1b10-43f4-b991-856b612060e0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:00:51.158Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d97b3e13daa5439","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
