t\n52\t- A documented crypto-module inventory exists for every Platform Operator\n53\t  image, and every non-validated usage is identified.\n54\t- A re-audit of the rebuilt images shows zero non-validated crypto usage in the\n55\t  operator's control/request path.\n56\t- The operator deploys and manages the model serving stack successfully on a\n57\t  FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, verified by functional tests.\n58\t- All rebuilt Platform Operator images pass their builds in the existing build\n59\t  pipeline.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled\n64\t  clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the\n65\t  request path) — this epic delivers that requirement for the Platform Operator\n66\t  images and for stack deployment under FIPS.\n67\t\n68\t## Risks / Notes\n69\t\n70\t- The strategy lists Platform Operator as an affected component but does not\n71\t  describe what changes; the scope above is the minimal functional reading\n72\t  (operator images free of non-validated crypto, stack deployable on FIPS\n73\t  clusters). Confirm with the strategy author.\n74\t- The Platform Operator has no architecture-context file; treat its build and\n75\t  onboarding status as unverified until one is added.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba6bdb076c1a8734","agent_id":"aa3a3d7aa4fa82aba","session_id":"06dfd5f6-e298-413b-a31d-879a10490586","uuid":"4f28fc6a-77d3-4719-888f-c08bd4ed7c96","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:00:51.744Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b34e5d87fa130faf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
