{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac1e4dccabaa6ca0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n3\ttitle: CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAdd a gating CI check that fails any model-serving-stack image build which\n34\treintroduces non-validated crypto usage, so that FIPS compliance cannot regress\n35\tonce the remediated images ship. The check is developed in parallel with the\n36\timage remediation work; its coupling to that work is expressed through\n37\tacceptance criteria, not through a scheduling dependency.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Implement detection of non-validated crypto-library linkage in\n42\t  serving-stack image builds (the detection rules align with the\n43\t  validated-module inventory established by the serving-stack image audit).\n44\t- Wire the check into the CI build pipelines owned by this epic's team so it\n45\t  runs on every KServe serving-stack image build.\n46\t- Make the check gating: a build that fails it cannot merge/ship.\n47\t- Provide a negative test fixture (a build that links a known non-validated\n48\t  crypto library) to prove the check fires, and a clean build to prove it\n49\t  passes.\n50\t- Time the activation of the gating behavior so it does not fail builds that\n51\t  predate the remediated images (advisory first, gating once remediation\n52\t  lands).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The check runs automatically on every KServe serving-stack image build in\n57\t  CI pipelines owned by RHOAI Serving.\n58\t- A build that links non-validated crypto in the request path fails the check,\n59\t  demonstrated by the negative test fixture.\n60\t- A build using only validated crypto modules passes the check.\n61\t- The check is gating, not advisory, at activation time.\n62\t- The check's detection rules cover every class of non-validated crypto usage\n63\t  identified by the serving-stack image audit (this criterion, not a DAG edge,\n64\t  is what couples the check to the remediation's findings).\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: CI enforces FIPS regressions — a gating check fails any\n69\t  serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-3's \"any serving-stack build\" spans build pipelines owned by more than\n74\t  one team. This epic delivers the gate for the KServe serving-stack image\n75\t  builds in the CI pipelines owned by RHOAI Serving. Wiring the same check\n76\t  into the Platform Operator build pipeline is coordinated work with RHOAI\n77\t  Platform Operators, who own that pipeline and the operator images — it is\n78\t  not a deliverable of this epic, and no dependency on their work is implied.\n79\t  Track that wiring as a cross-team follow-up when scheduling.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba6bdb076c1a8734","agent_id":"aa3a3d7aa4fa82aba","session_id":"06dfd5f6-e298-413b-a31d-879a10490586","uuid":"7fb3e835-789c-4289-8d2f-ba2ab4e0f96b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:00:54.803Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac1e4dccabaa6ca0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]