e Platform Operator image builds — which this same decomposition counts as\nserving-stack images under HLR-1 (E002) — have no epic delivering the gate:\nE003 explicitly disclaims it and E002's scope does not include it. Platform\nOperator is an in-declared-scope component, so this is a P1 coverage gap, not\na scope-boundary deferral. Correction: add the operator-pipeline wiring to\nE002's scope, or create a small epic assigned to RHOAI Platform Operators\nthat wires the check into their build pipeline.\n\nOne ambiguity properly flagged (minor, no score impact beyond the above): the\nproblem statement asserts \"the serving data plane link[s] non-validated crypto\nlibraries\" and HLR-1 says \"all serving-stack images\", but the strategy's\nAffected Components list declares only KServe and Platform Operator. The\ndecomposition defers the Serving Runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit — named as\nthe model-execution data plane in `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`)\nwith a thorough justification and a confirmation recommendation (Health\nWarning 3). Because the deferral follows the strategy's declared component\nlist and the contradiction originates in the strategy itself, this is a\nflagged ambiguity, not a missing P0 HLR. The confirmation with the strategy\nauthor must happen before execution; if the deferral is not intended, add a\nServing Runtimes remediation epic mirroring E001 (and extend HLR-3's gate\ncoverage accordingly).\n\n### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n\nDiagram and frontmatter match exactly: diagram edges {E001→E004, E002→E004,\nE001→E005, E002→E005, E003→E005, E004→E005} correspond one-to-one with\nE004's dependencies [E001, E002] and E005's dependencies [E001, E002, E003,\nE004]; E001/E002/E003 have none. Arrows run dependency → dependent per the\nconvention. No cycles. Critical path length 3 (E001/E002 → E004 → E005) is\nwithin the M-strategy heuristic (3-4).\n\nEvery edge is justified: E001/E002 → E004 under Rule 13 (the evidence package\nis assembled from the remediations' inventories and test results as content\nthe consumer cannot precede); all four edges into E005 under Rule 11\n(docs-authoring blocked by every Implementation epic). Parallelism is handled\nexactly right: E003 ∥ E001/E002 with the coupling to the audit findings\nexpressed as an AC on E003 (Rule 13 configuration reference), and E004 ∥ the\nbuild pipelines with attestations consumed as content via an AC — both are\nthe rule-compliant shapes, and their absence from the DAG is correct. No\nkonflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics exist, so\nRules 7/8/10 are not implicated. No conditional branch files. No\ndata/artifact dependency discoverable from epic content is missing from the\nDAG.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n\nComponent/team tuples are separated correctly: E001 (KServe / RHOAI Serving),\nE002 (Platform Operator / RHOAI Platform Operators), E003 (KServe / RHOAI\nServing, CI configuration — distinct surface from E001), E004 (evidence\nassembly and submission — one logical deliverable, correctly not split by\ncomponent since there is one package and one submission), E005\n(Documentation / docs-authoring — content authoring correctly separated from\ncode work per the work-product boundary). No scope duplication: E001 and\nE002 apply the same remediation pattern to different components' images, and\nE003's detection work does not rebuild E001's audit.\n\nE001's potential overage against the ~2-week guideline is handled per the\nrubric: Health Warning 6 records a concrete re-split trigger (\"re-split E001\nalong image or sub-system lines if the audit finds materially more affected\nimages or crypto-linkage sites than the strategy's 'several images' estimate\nsuggests\"), extended to E002. A triggered, justified overage — this is a\nsingle mechanical pass over one surface where a split would duplicate the\naudit — so the criterion is not docked.\n\nObservation (not an issue): E004's `component: KServe