tes (\"producing\npipeline attestations\") beyond what kserve.md literally states, but the\ngrounding (Konflux onboarded: yes) is real — not a calibration miss.\nComputed `ai_implementability` fields were not checked, per pipeline\nownership of that arithmetic.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n\nEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy. Rule-mandated ACs are\npresent: E005 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review-against-implementation\nAC; E001/E002/E003 carry build-pipeline-green ACs; no konflux chain exists,\nso Rule 25 is satisfied vacuously. E001/E002 are hardening changes, not\ncapability replacements, so no rollback/feature-flag AC is triggered.\n\nSoft-AC scan: clean. The externally controlled constraints — the lab's\nsix-to-nine-month turnaround, the review-board cadence, lab triage, and the\ncertification decision itself — are all recorded in E004's Risks/Notes and\nHealth Warning 5, not as ACs. E004's submission AC is a valid condition on\nthe epic's own deliverable (a complete package submitted), not a\nprecondition granted by others. No epic body references sibling epics by\ndraft ID.\n\n### 7. Completeness (1/2)\n\nCore scope is fully accounted for: FIPS remediation of both declared\ncomponents (E001, E002), the evidence package and submission path (E004),\nCI regression enforcement (E003), documentation (E005). Strategy-level\ncontext is carried forward, not dropped: the externally controlled gates are\nin E004's risks and Health Warning 5, the missing strategy sections are\nflagged (Health Warning 1), team assumptions are flagged (Health Warning 2),\nand tiered delivery is analyzed. Out-of-scope items (workbenches, pipelines,\ntraining, Common Criteria) are correctly excluded.\n\nOne minor scope gap, the same root cause as the Criterion 1 finding: the\nwiring of the FIPS regression gate into the Platform Operator build pipeline\nis a capability slice of HLR-3 that no epic delivers — it is documented as a\ncross-team follow-up on E003's risks, which accounts for it but does not\ncover it. Correction: fold it into E002's scope or add an epic assigned to\nRHOAI Platform Operators. The Serving Runtimes deferral is a documented\nscope-boundary decision pending author confirmation (see Criterion 1), not a\nsilent drop.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44156,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba6bdb076c1a8734","agent_id":"aa3a3d7aa4fa82aba","session_id":"06dfd5f6-e298-413b-a31d-879a10490586","uuid":"3af06589-e43d-4740-8ffb-12c095e68e44","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:05:26.559Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
